9-10-2026 Github Copilot for Testing and Refactoring

(Slide 3 as an overview)

AAA Template for Status
    - Arrange
    - Act
    - Assert

Generating Edge Cases
    - Ensures code is robust and works correctly under unusual or unexpected conditions
    - one behavior, one assertion, one clear name

    - Know your boundaries
    - Think like a user
        - how might they misuse it
    - Happy and Sad Paths
        - Success and failure scenarios
    - Review and Refine

Generating Mock Objects
    - Suggests the right mock objects for your dependencies
    - Generates stubs with default or custom return values
    - Sets up interactions - calls, arguments, order
    - Helps mock, exceptions, timeouts, and failures

Verifying Mock Interactions
    - verify() confirms a call actually happened - not just that the code compiled
    - times(1) and never() catch missing or duplicate calls

Refactor in small, tested steps - confirm behavior is unchanged before and after every change.

Refactoring Quality
    - Naming and Clarity
    - Method/Class Size
    - Duplication
    - Coupling and Abstractions
    - Domain Types (Slide 29)
        - Use value objects and enums, not raw primitives
        - public enum CustomerStatus{PROSPECT, ACTIVE, SUSPENDED, CLOSED}
    - Tests and Behavior Preservation

